# NOT APPLIED -- the user deferred this ("2 先算了"). Kept so the work is not lost.
#
# WHAT IT IS: the gmd_dev left-basis (Q0/qrows/Q) half of the receive-combiner
# offload. With this, gmd_k can emit q_gmd and ucd_k can emit w_ucd, so the
# receive combiner stops being PS-only. It is the kernel half ONLY: the
# runtime wrappers (Runtime::gmd_op / ucd_op need U/urows/Q parameters), the
# decomp_main gates (e_Q is currently compared for strat==3 only, although
# tools/decomp_ref.py already ships q_gmd and w_ucd for strats 1 and 2) and the
# registry/xclbin call-site updates are NOT in this diff.
#
# SCOPE OF THIS DIFF: the gmd_dev core only (Q0/qrows/Q plumbing: the entry
# copy, the pivot swap in lockstep with P, and the g2 left-Givens transcribed
# from ref/decomp.cpp). The gmd_k/ucd_k signature changes that would expose it
# (U/qrows/Q on gmd_k; U/urows/Q = w_ucd on ucd_k, with left_scale =
# sqrt(pl)*sg/saug and production's safe_diagonal floor) were written and
# syntax-checked too but are NOT in this file -- re-derive them from
# ref/decomp.cpp::gmd_factors and ref/rx.cpp's 'u' branch, which are the
# authority for the formulas.
#
# STATUS: syntax-checked with `clang -x cl -cl-std=CL1.2 -fsyntax-only` and
# nothing more. The NUMERICS ARE UNVERIFIED -- decomp_bench has never run this
# code, so do not assume the left-Givens transcription from ref/decomp.cpp's
# gmd_factors is right until e_Q for strats 1 and 2 is gated against the oracle.
#
# WHY IT WAS DEFERRED, with the number that justifies deferring: the combiner is
# ~us of work against a 1.2 ms null-basis kernel event at the largest pool shape,
# so offloading it buys nothing today. It becomes worth finishing only if a
# deployment wants the WHOLE instant on the fabric with no PS round trip.
#
# To apply: patch -p1 < docs/ucd_q_kernel.patch   (paths are a/kernels/decomp.cl)
--- a/kernels/decomp.cl	2026-10-25 23:51:21
+++ b/kernels/decomp.cl	2026-10-25 23:51:22
@@ -256,8 +256,10 @@
